  <h1>GLP-1 in France (2026): Prices, Prescriptions and Rules — in English</h1>
  <p>Moving to France, or staying long-term, while on a GLP-1 medication? Good news first: <strong>France has some of the lowest regulated GLP-1 prices in the world</strong>, and since June 2026 the national health insurance even reimburses 65% of Wegovy and Mounjaro for eligible patients. Here is how the French system actually works, written for English speakers.</p>

  <h2>Prices: regulated, identical in every pharmacy</h2>
  <p>Unlike the United States, medication prices in France are set by the government (CEPS). Every pharmacy in the country charges exactly the same price — there is no shopping around, no coupons, no pharmacy markup:</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Medication</th><th>Price in France / month</th><th>US list price / month*</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Wegovy (semaglutide) 0.25–1 mg</td><td>€146.91</td><td rowspan="2">$1,350</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Wegovy 2.4 mg (maintenance)</td><td>€195.10</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mounjaro (tirzepatide) 2.5 mg</td><td>€176.10</td><td rowspan="2">≈ $1,069</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mounjaro 12.5–15 mg</td><td>€433.80</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Ozempic (diabetes only)</td><td>€77.60</td><td>≈ $1,000+</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p style="font-size:0.85em;color:#666;">*US list prices before insurance, per <a href="https://www.goodrx.com/wegovy/wegovy-for-weight-loss-cost-coverage" rel="nofollow">GoodRx</a> (2026). US manufacturer cash-pay programs offer lower prices (~$199–349/month for Wegovy), still above the French regulated price at most doses. Note: tirzepatide is sold in France under the brand Mounjaro.</p>

  <h2>Prescriptions: you need a doctor practicing in France</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>US, UK or other non-EU prescriptions are not valid</strong> in French pharmacies.</li>
    <li>A prescription from another <strong>EU/EEA country</strong> is generally accepted under EU cross-border prescription rules (Directive 2011/24/EU).</li>
    <li>The practical path: book a French GP (médecin généraliste) — any doctor can prescribe GLP-1 medications for obesity since June 2025. Doctolib works in English for finding doctors.</li>
    <li>All GLP-1s are prescription-only. Websites selling them without a prescription are selling counterfeits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reimbursement: 65% — but only inside the French health system</h2>
  <p>Since <strong>June 15, 2026</strong>, French national health insurance covers 65% of Wegovy and Mounjaro for obesity under strict conditions: BMI ≥ 40, or BMI ≥ 35 with a weight-related comorbidity (type 2 diabetes, hypertension, sleep apnea…), after 6 months of documented nutritional care, and the <strong>initial reimbursed prescription must come from a specialist obesity center (CSO/CHU)</strong> — your GP can then renew it. You need to be affiliated with French social security (carte Vitale). If you are not (yet) in the system, you pay the regulated price out of pocket — which is still a fraction of US prices.</p>

